 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 511125,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Use the slope formula to find the slope of the line through the pair of points <span data-math=\"(-3, 4)\">(-3, 4)</span> and <span data-math=\"(2, -1)\">(2, -1)</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Point 1: (–3, 4) and Point 2: (2, –1).</p>\n<p>Find the slope.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"m = \\frac{{{y_2} - {y_1}}}{{{x_2} - {x_1}}} = \\frac{{2 - \\left( { - 3} \\right)}}{{ - 1 - 4}}\"></span></td>\n<td>Substitute.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"m = \\frac{5}{{ - 5}} = - 1\"></span></td>\n<td>Simplify.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The slope is –1.</p>\n<p>You can plot the points and verify the slope by counting the rise over the run.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{\\text{slope}} = - 1\">{\\text{slope}} = - 1</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
